            {{-- Sheaf's main asks for a screen of height, which is a screen too
                 much in this variant: the grid already spent a header on the row
                 above, and the layout clips what does not fit. Sized to its own
                 row instead, and made a column so a page that sizes itself
                 against the viewport — the kit's dashboard does — has a height to
                 measure. The child is where the 6/8 the kit's own main gave its
                 pages comes back; Sheaf pads main's children by 2 with a selector
                 a plain utility loses to, hence the important. --}}
            <x-ui.layout.main class="flex flex-col min-h-0! max-h-full!">
